    "id": "hf-5962",
    "crop": "Potato",
    "instruction": "How does common scab spread and survive in potato plants?",
    "advisory": "The pathogen attacks various crops such as cabbage, carrot, eggplant, onion, radish, spinach, and turnip. It perpetuates in soil and infects the crop every year. Infected potato tubers serve as the main source of long-distance spread of the disease. The pathogen may survive passage through the digestive tract of animals and hence may spread with farmyard manure.",
