    "id": "hf-5963",
    "crop": "Potato",
    "instruction": "What management practices can be implemented to control common scab in potato plants?",
    "advisory": "Plant only scab-free seed potatoes to check the spread of the inoculum and infection in subsequent crops. Infection of seed tubers can be removed by a 1.5-hour dip in 0.1% mercuric chloride solution or a 2-hour dip in a solution of 1 part formaldehyde in 240 parts of water. Soil application of PCNB at the time of planting can reduce the disease. Four to six years of crop rotation with alfalfa is satisfactory under irrigated conditions. The disease incidence can be effectively reduced by green manuring the fields before planting potatoes. Common scab is severe in alkaline soil, so the application of alkaline fertilizers like calcium ammonium nitrate should be avoided.",
