    "instruction": "Demonstrate the procedure for preparing a one kattha nursery bed for growing germinated paddy seeds.",
    "advisory": "To prepare a one katta nursery bed for growing germinated paddy seeds, follow these steps:\n \n\n 1. Select and Prepare the Location:\n Choose a flat, well-drained area with access to sunlight and water. The bed should be 5 feet in width and 6 feet in length. The bed height should be 4 inches above ground level. Create a surrounding drain that is 18 inches wide and 8 inches deep for proper water management. Clear any weeds or debris.\n \n\n 2. Soil Preparation:\n Loosen the soil using a hoe or kurpi. Ensure that the soil is well-aerated and free from large clumps.\n \n\n 3. Add Organic Matter:\n Evenly spread 1 kilogram of vermicompost and 1 basket of decomposed cow dung over the soil. Mix these amendments thoroughly into the top layer to improve fertility.\n \n\n 4. Level the Bed:\n Smooth and level the soil using a hoe to create an even bed for uniform water distribution.\n \n\n 5. Sow the Sprouted Seeds:\n Evenly spread 100 grams of sprouted paddy seeds over the prepared bed. Make sure they’re not clustered too closely to prevent overcrowding. Cover the nursery bed with straw to prevent birds from eating the seeds and to help retain moisture in the soil. Remove the straw after 3 days.\n \n\n 6. Watering:\n Gently water the bed using a shower watering can regularly. Avoid excessive watering; maintain consistent moisture for optimal germination.",
