    "instruction": "Zinc deficiency in wheat plants can be identified by the following symptoms:\n- Leaves turn yellow along the veins while the veins remain green.\n- In severe deficiency, leaves show mottled stripes and oily spots.\n- These symptoms are found in small, specific areas and start from the third or fourth leaf stage.\n\nHere are some follow-up questions you can ask:\n1. How can I treat zinc deficiency in wheat plants?\n2. What causes zinc deficiency in wheat crops?\n3. Are there any preventive measures to avoid zinc deficiency in wheat farming?",
