    "id": "hf-7194",
    "crop": "Mango",
    "instruction": "To prepare mango saplings, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Collect mango seeds: Obtain fresh mango seeds from ripe mango fruits.\n\n2. Remove the outer husk: Carefully remove the outer husk of the mango seed using a knife or by rubbing it gently.\n\n3. Prepare the planting medium: Create a mixture of farmyard manure, red soil, and sand. Alternatively, you can use polythene bags filled with a similar mixture.\n\n4. Sow the seeds: Plant the mango seeds in the prepared planting medium, either directly in the raised beds or in polythene bags. Ensure that the seeds are sown within 4-5 weeks after extraction to maintain their viability.\n\n5. Provide proper care: Water the young plants regularly, especially those up to 2 years old. Newly-planted grafts require about 30 liters of water every week. Irrigate the grown-up trees at regular intervals, particularly after fruit set, to increase yield.\n\nHere are some follow-up questions you can ask:\n\n1. What is the ideal time to sow mango seeds?\n2. How long does it take for mango seeds to germinate?\n3. Can I use any type of soil for planting mango seeds?",
