    "crop": "Garlic",
    "instruction": "To remove yellowness in garlic plants, you can try the following solutions:\n\n- Apply a solution of Zinc Sulfate: Zinc Sulfate is an effective remedy for zinc deficiency in plants. Prepare a solution by mixing Zinc Sulfate at a rate of 2.5 to 3 grams per liter of water. Spray this solution on the garlic plants to provide them with the necessary zinc nutrients.\n\n- Use Zinc chelates: Although more expensive than inorganic zinc sources, zinc chelates can also be used to address zinc deficiency in plants. However, their purity may be uncertain.\n\n- Ensure proper drainage: Poor drainage can contribute to nutrient deficiencies and yellowing in plants. Make sure the soil has good drainage to prevent waterlogging and promote healthy growth.\n\nHere are some follow-up questions you can ask:\n\n1. How often should I apply the Zinc Sulfate solution to garlic plants?\n2. Are there any other symptoms of zinc deficiency in plants besides yellowness?\n3. Can I use other zinc sources besides Zinc Sulfate and zinc chelates to address zinc deficiency in garlic plants?",
