    "instruction": "लता, if you cultivate green chillies and the leaves turn yellow and dry up, it could be due to a disease or pest infestation. Here are some possible causes and control measures:\n\n1. Disease: Powdery mildew\n   - Symptoms: Leaves form dark brown powder, shrink, and dry.\n   - Control: Spray Myclobutanil 1Gram/L or soluble Sulphur at 0.3% for spraying.\n\n2. Disease: Leaf Curl\n   - Symptoms: Leaves enlarge, crinkle, and become thicker and leathery.\n   - Control: Treat seeds with imidacloprid 70 WS@ 5ml/kg and foliar spray appropriate insecticides.\n\n3. Disease: Collar Rot or Foot Rot\n   - Symptoms: Stem rots near the ground surface, white fungus grows on the rotten part.\n   - Control: Use healthy seeds, treat seeds with fungicides, perform deep plowing in summer, destroy crop residues, and ensure proper drainage.\n\nHere are some follow-up questions you can ask:\n1. How can I prevent powdery mildew in my green chilli plants?\n2. What are the symptoms of leaf curl disease in green chillies?\n3. How can I control collar rot or foot rot in my green chilli plants?\n\nRemember, these answers are based on the information provided in the context.",
