    "instruction": "Verticillium lecanii is a beneficial fungus that can be used for pest control in farming. Here's how you can use it:\n\n- Mix 5 grams or 5 ml of Verticillium lecanii per liter of water for pest control.\n- Spray the mixture on the affected plants or areas where pests are present.\n- The fungus grows as mycelium inside the pest's body and produces a toxin called \"cyclopeptides\" which kills the pest.\n- The fungus can kill pests within 2-3 days, depending on environmental conditions.\n- To ensure the quality of the product, make sure it contains x10⁶ cfu (Colony Forming Units) per gram of the substance.\n\nExamples of follow-up questions:\n1. How does Verticillium lecanii kill pests?\n2. What are the environmental conditions required for the effective use of Verticillium lecanii?\n3. Can Verticillium lecanii be used for pest control in all types of crops?",
