    "crop": "Chickpea",
    "instruction": "Krishna: How can I control fungal diseases in my crops?\n\nVistaar: To control fungal diseases in crops, you can follow these measures:\n- Crop rotation can be used to control fungal diseases to some extent.\n- Treat the seeds with 0.3% Thiram or Captain at 2 grams per kg before sowing.\n- Ensure timely irrigation for crops in the summer.\n- Proper drainage management should be implemented during the rainy season.\n- Use Validamycin 2 grams/liter or Tebuconazole 1 gram per liter of water for soil irrigation.\n- For specific diseases like powdery mildew, use Myclobutanil 1Gram/L or soluble Sulphur at 0.3% for spraying.\n\nHere are some follow-up questions you can ask:\n1. How does crop rotation help in controlling fungal diseases?\n2. Can you provide more details about treating seeds with Thiram or Captain?\n3. What are the symptoms of powdery mildew and how does it spread?",
